# PATCH-2026-09-27 — registry capability clobber (ROOT CAUSE + FIX)

## Root cause (verified 2026-09-27 against live qnfo-ops/worker.js, 354,616 bytes)

1. `qnfo-ops/worker.js:4323` — `manifest()` returns a HARD-CODED capabilities array
   (48 entries, ending `"websocket-hibernation"`). It does NOT include
   `d1-schema-index` or `guard-registry`.
2. `qnfo-ops/worker.js:4351` — self-registration calls
   `upsert("qnfo-ops", "worker", { ..., capabilities: manifest().capabilities, ... })`.
3. `qnfo-ops/worker.js:4238` (and `:4347`) — the upsert does
   `capabilities=excluded.capabilities` — i.e. **REPLACE, not MERGE**.

Consequence: any capability written into `service_registry.capabilities` by
anything other than the worker's own manifest is silently destroyed on the next
self-registration (deploy, cron, or health path). Observed in production:
`d1-schema-index` was written at 2026-09-27T04:50Z and was gone by
2026-09-27T19:00Z (row then read `2.37.14-callglm-reasoning`).

This is a general defect, not a one-off: it applies to EVERY out-of-band
capability advertisement for EVERY worker that uses this upsert.

## Fix (minimum, one line)

```diff
--- a/qnfo-ops/worker.js
+++ b/qnfo-ops/worker.js
@@ -4323,7 +4323,10 @@
-    capabilities: ["ops-ai-gateway", "openai-compatible", "chat", "agent", "code", "tool-execution", "fleet-probes", "full-fleet-probes", "multi-db-query", "vectorize-search", "r2-access", "kv-access", "research-queue", "queue-query", "analytics", "self-registration", "service-registry", "capability-advertising-audit", "telemetry", "self-heal", "isolated-ops-logging", "pure-server-exec", "streamed-answers", "async-jobs", "run-to-completion", "self-chaining-jobs", "workspace-edit", "workspace-grep", "workspace-glob", "workspace-diff", "workspace-patch", "run-code-net", "exec-pipeline", "git-ops", "parallel-reads", "claude-code-parity", "full-stack-shell", "cloudflare-containers", "real-python-interpreter", "real-node-interpreter", "bash-execution", "pip-install", "npm-install", "git-clone", "firecracker-vm", "agents-sdk", "durable-agent-sessions", "websocket-hibernation"],
+    capabilities: ["ops-ai-gateway", "openai-compatible", "chat", "agent", "code", "tool-execution", "fleet-probes", "full-fleet-probes", "multi-db-query", "vectorize-search", "r2-access", "kv-access", "research-queue", "queue-query", "analytics", "self-registration", "service-registry", "capability-advertising-audit", "telemetry", "self-heal", "isolated-ops-logging", "pure-server-exec", "streamed-answers", "async-jobs", "run-to-completion", "self-chaining-jobs", "workspace-edit", "workspace-grep", "workspace-glob", "workspace-diff", "workspace-patch", "run-code-net", "exec-pipeline", "git-ops", "parallel-reads", "claude-code-parity", "full-stack-shell", "cloudflare-containers", "real-python-interpreter", "real-node-interpreter", "bash-execution", "pip-install", "npm-install", "git-clone", "firecracker-vm", "agents-sdk", "durable-agent-sessions", "websocket-hibernation", "d1-schema-index", "guard-registry", "schema-drift-check"],
```

## Fix (structural, preferred — stops the class of bug)

Make the self-registration MERGE advertised capabilities instead of replacing
them, so out-of-band capabilities survive. Either:

(a) SQL side — change `capabilities=excluded.capabilities` to a union in the
    upsert at `:4238`/`:4347`; or
(b) worker side — before upsert, read the existing row and union its
    `capabilities` with `manifest().capabilities`.

Option (a) is a one-token change but SQLite cannot union JSON arrays without
json_each/json_group_array gymnastics inside the upsert; option (b) is more code
but far clearer and testable.

## Verification for whoever applies this

1. Deploy, then confirm: `SELECT capabilities FROM service_registry WHERE service='qnfo-ops'`
   contains `d1-schema-index` and `guard-registry`.
2. Force a second self-registration (hit the health/registration path again).
3. Re-run step 1. If the capabilities are still present, the merge fix works.
   If they vanish, only the manifest line was applied and the class of bug remains.

## Do-not-retry note

Deploying this patch from the ops endpoint itself is NOT safe:
`cf_worker_read` returns a TRUNCATED bundle (`bundle_snippet` cut mid-template-
literal at 40k chars), and `cf_worker_deploy` requires the full inline source.
Deploying a fragment would destroy the live worker. Apply via the repo's normal
deploy path instead.
